   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "וְטָרִית שֶׁאֵינָהּ טְרוּפָה: תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן, אֵיזוֹ הִיא טָרִית שֶׁאֵינָהּ טְרוּפָה? כֹּל שֶׁרֹאשׁ וְשִׁדְרָה נִיכָּר. וְאֵיזוֹ צִיר שֶׁיֵּשׁ בָּהּ דָּגָה? כָּל שֶׁכִּילְבִּית אַחַת אוֹ שְׁתֵּי כִּילְבִּיּוֹת",
   "en": "§ The mishna further teaches: «And tarit» fish «that is not minced» and brine that has fish in it are permitted. «The Sages taught: What is» considered «tarit that has not been minced? Any» fish whose «head and spine are recognizable. And what is» considered «brine that has fish in it? Any» brine «that» has «one kilbit or two kilbiyot»"
  }
